---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import TranslationNotice from '../../components/TranslationNotice.astro';

/* Английская редакция `/terms`, построена 2026-08-26. Источник содержания —
 * `docs/legal/public/terms.md`, редакция 1.2 от 2026-08-25, та же редакция и
 * дата, что у русской страницы `/terms`. Оговорка о приоритете
 * (`TranslationNotice`) — сразу после заголовка. */
---
<Base title="Terms of Service — wfeels"
      description="Terms of use for wfeels.site and how an individual contract is concluded."
      noindex={true}>
  <Container>
    <Section>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Terms of Service</h1>
      <TranslationNotice ruHref="/terms" />
      <style>
        /* На 390 px (мобильный класс раскладки, `WIDTHS_OTHER` в `font-
         * fallback-metrics.spec.ts`) контейнер `h1` — 358 px (`Container`,
         * `padding-inline: 16px` с обеих сторон), а натуральная ширина
         * фразы без переноса (замер `getBoundingClientRect()` на
         * `white-space: nowrap`, 36 px — минимум клэмпа `.t-h1` до 642 px
         * ширины экрана) — 353,95 px на запасном начертании и 372,56 px на
         * настоящем Unbounded: контейнер попадает МЕЖДУ этими числами,
         * фраза держится в одну строку на фолбэке и переносится на
         * настоящем шрифте. Скачок высоты — ровно одна строка `t-h1`
         * (39,59 px, `line-height: 1.1` × 36 px), тот же класс дефекта, что
         * уже сводили 2026-08-23 на девяти русских посадочных и на
         * `/terms` (`ServiceHero.astro`, `[slug].astro`).
         *
         * Приём тот же: не пиксель, а `em`, чтобы граница переноса держалась
         * той же долей от кегля на всей полосе, где кегль не меняется
         * (≤479 px, тот же порог, что у переноса `.t-h1` в `base.css`).
         * 7em = 252 px на 36 px кегле — с запасом ниже обеих натуральных
         * ширин «Terms of» (197,84 px на настоящем шрифте, 182,42 px на
         * фолбэке) и выше обеих натуральных ширин «Service» (167,67 px /
         * 158,63 px), так что перенос идёт в одной и той же точке — после
         * «of» — независимо от того, какое начертание сейчас на экране. */
        @media (max-width: 479px) {
          h1 { max-width: 7em; }
        }
      </style>
      <Prose>
        <p><strong>Revision 1.2 of 25 August 2026.</strong></p>

        <h2>1. Provider</h2>
        <p>
          Сабуров Даниил Денисович, Tax ID <code>183700967882</code>, a
          self-employed individual under the special tax regime
          «Professional Income Tax», not registered as a sole trader. Place
          of business — Saint Petersburg. Email for contracts, enquiries
          and claims: <a href="mailto:i@dsaburov.ru">i@dsaburov.ru</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Status of the information on the site</h2>
        <p>
          2.1. The site contains information about experience, services,
          the possible scope of work, and indicative prices and timelines.
        </p>
        <p>
          2.2. The site, its pages, form messages, and prices shown as
          «from» do not constitute a public offer. They do not obligate the
          Provider to conclude a contract with anyone who gets in touch.
        </p>
        <p>
          2.3. Under the model used here, a Contract is concluded after the
          task has been discussed, an individual specification, price,
          timeline and stages have been agreed, and the parties have signed
          a separate document. Submitting the enquiry form is not, by
          itself, acceptance. That said, an actual exchange of messages can
          form a contract if the parties clearly and unambiguously agreed
          all material terms and followed whatever form they chose;
          legally significant messages are therefore worded without
          ambiguity.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Services</h2>
        <p>
          The Provider builds and improves websites, software solutions,
          automations, integrations, backend systems, Telegram bots and
          Mini Apps, carries out audits, and provides agreed support. The
          exact deliverable and scope of work are always defined in an
          individual contract and specification.
        </p>
        <p>
          Client materials, content migration, domain, hosting, licences,
          subscriptions, payment-system fees, AI model costs and
          third-party services are included in the price only when the
          specification says so explicitly. As a general rule, domains,
          hosting, licences and accounts are registered to and paid for
          directly by the client.
        </p>

        <h2>4. How a deal is concluded</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>The client sends an enquiry or gets in touch through the contact given.</li>
          <li>The parties clarify the goal, source materials, deliverable and constraints.</li>
          <li>The Provider sends a proposal and a draft specification.</li>
          <li>The parties sign an individual contract and its specification annex.</li>
          <li>Once signed, the Provider issues an invoice and payment details, or sends an individual «Request Money» request from the T-Bank app, linked to the contract and stage.</li>
          <li>The Provider starts work once the first payment required by the contract and the necessary materials have been received.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Exchanging signed PDFs from agreed email addresses, or another
          method of electronic signature explicitly named in the contract,
          is acceptable.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Price and payment</h2>
        <p>
          The final price is set once the task has been reviewed and is
          fixed in the contract or specification.
        </p>
        <p>Unless the parties agree a different schedule:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>for a total price under <code>70 000 ₽</code> — 50% once the estimate is agreed and the contract is signed, before work starts; the remaining 50% — after delivery, under the contract, and before launch;</li>
          <li>for a price of <code>70 000 ₽</code> or more — payment by the milestones set out in the specification.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Any prepayment is an advance, not a deposit. For each payment
          received, the Provider issues a self-employed tax receipt through
          the My Tax app and passes it to the client. A corporate or
          sole-trader client provides the correct Tax ID for the receipt.
        </p>
        <p>
          The payment procedure, purpose and deadline are set out in the
          individual contract, the invoice, or the personal transfer
          request.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Performance and changes</h2>
        <p>
          6.1. The client provides lawful materials, access and decisions
          needed for the work in good time. A delay on the client's part
          may push the deadline back by the corresponding period plus a
          reasonable time to resume the task.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.2. The Provider shows interim results in the manner set out in
          the specification.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.3. Changing the deliverable, its scope, integrations, page
          count, scenarios, or the number of revision rounds is done in
          writing. Extra work does not start until the new price and
          deadline are agreed.
        </p>
        <p>
          6.4. The use of software tools and artificial-intelligence
          systems is allowed under the Provider's supervision. The
          client's confidential and personal data is not passed to an
          external system without an agreed basis for doing so.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Acceptance and delivery of the result</h2>
        <p>
          The procedure for demonstration, review, comments and acceptance
          is set out in the contract. A substantiated objection is one that
          points to a specific discrepancy with the specification. New
          requests are not a defect and are priced separately.
        </p>
        <p>
          The result is delivered electronically. Source files,
          instructions and access are handed over to the extent set out in
          the specification. The channel and scope of delivery are recorded
          in the contract, an acceptance report, or related correspondence.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Warranty fixes</h2>
        <p>
          Within 30 calendar days of acceptance, the Provider fixes, free of
          charge, reproducible discrepancies between the result and the
          agreed specification, unless they arose from changes made by the
          client, a third party, an external platform, or a failure to
          follow instructions.
        </p>
        <p>
          New features, new content, design or integration changes,
          external API updates, and the consequences of third-party
          interference are billed separately. The client's statutory rights
          concerning defects are not limited by this commercial warranty.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          Rights to a specially created result are transferred or granted
          to the extent, and at the point, stated in the contract, usually
          after the corresponding stage is paid in full.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rights to third-party libraries, fonts, images, platforms and
          other components are governed by their own rights holders'
          licences. The Provider's own general-purpose work created earlier
          is not transferred unless the contract explicitly says otherwise;
          the client receives a sufficient right to use it as part of the
          paid result.
        </p>
        <p>
          Publishing the logo, interface or commercial materials of a
          project requires the separate permission of the rights holder.
          Publishing the name, position, image, quote or testimonial of an
          identifiable individual requires that person's own separate
          consent to the disclosure of personal data; the client's
          permission does not substitute for it.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Termination and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          The procedure for terminating the contract, settling the
          completed part, and any refund is governed by the individual
          contract and applicable law. A prepayment is not declared
          unconditionally non-refundable. A refund calculation is set out
          in writing, taking into account the work actually performed and
          applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Personal data</h2>
        <p>
          Processing of visitors' and enquirers' data is described in the{' '}
          <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. The separate consent for
          the form is at <a href="/en/consent">/en/consent</a>. Consent to
          advertising or to the portfolio is not included in consent to
          process an enquiry.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Claims</h2>
        <p>
          A claim is sent to <a href="mailto:i@dsaburov.ru">i@dsaburov.ru</a>{' '}
          with a description of the demand, the contract number, and any
          relevant materials. A reply is sent within the period required by
          law or the contract.
        </p>
        <p>
          The claims procedure does not limit an individual consumer's
          rights and does not deprive them of the right to go to court or
          to a government authority in the cases provided by law.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          A new revision applies to use of the site after the date it is
          published. The terms of a contract already signed are not
          changed by publishing a new page without the parties' agreement.
        </p>
      </Prose>
      <a href="/en#contact" class="back-to-form">
        <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to the form
      </a>
    </Section>
  </Container>
</Base>
